chunks.text:
[Playful]
{a mischievous, charming little waltz in 3/4 at 120 bpm in a minor key: pizzicato strings play a bouncing oom-pah-pah}
{a celesta and a glockenspiel play one short, catchy, hummable tune that repeats; a cheeky clarinet and a bassoon answer it}
{light, funny, tiptoeing, like a friendly little imp; no drums, no brass, nothing scary yet}

[Wedding]
{the same tune as a warm, elegant wedding waltz: lush legato strings, a harp and a soft horn, glowing and romantic}
{in the last two seconds one wrong, low, sour note from a contrabassoon and a low piano string sneaks in under it}

[Lullaby]
{the same tune, slow and tender, played alone on a small music box, a lullaby in a nursery at night}
{a low, uneasy bowed double-bass drone creeps in under it and slowly grows; one soft low brass note at the very end}

[Swagger]
{the same tune turned heavy and swaggering at half speed: low trombones and a tuba play it over a slow half-time kick and snare}
{sinister and confident, a deep gritty bass under it, low strings joining; it grows bigger and more threatening to the end}

[Horror]
{the same tune as full horror, very slow: massive deep brass blasts, a wordless dark choir, pounding giant drums, screeching strings}
{one colossal hit at 6 seconds, the biggest of all; then it keeps building, louder and louder, and stops dead on the last beat}
